// ⛔ THE SECOND SUITE MANIFEST LIVES HERE, and it was missing until an audit counted the
//    stores against docs/07 §2. That row does not say "draw the suite" — it says draw
//    EVERY store AND ITS WRITER, and it names this pair as the one that is NOT symmetric:
//    suite/benchmark/ has no writer at all once generated, suite/regression/ has exactly
//    one. Four statuses were drawn with no store under them, so the picture showed what a
//    case BECOMES and never where it is kept or who may put it there. A store with one
//    writer is a design claim; an undrawn store is that claim made invisible.
Life [color: grey, icon: repeat, label: "11 · the case lifecycle — P3.3–P3.6, DEFERRED (D-030)"] {
  MinePy [icon: filter, label: "loop/mine.py · loop/suite.py\nfailures → suite/proposed/"]
  // ⛔ THE FIVE ADMISSION GATES WERE A LINE OF TEXT INSIDE THIS LABEL, and the promotion
  //    gate's five conditions are five nodes on a chain. Same kind of object — an AND of
  //    mechanical checks — drawn two different ways, so only one of them read as a gate.
  //    A reader could not see that admission is also all-or-nothing, and a text list has no
  //    place to hang the thing that matters about gate 5: the `why` is required and there is
  //    still no human step (D-040). Structure is what makes the AND checkable.
  Admit [color: grey, icon: filter, label: "the five admission gates — ALL five, docs/02 §5"] {
    A1 [icon: repeat, label: "1 · reproducible"]
    A2 [icon: activity, label: "2 · not_flaky"]
    A3 [icon: slash, label: "3 · not_a_void"]
    A4 [icon: git-branch, label: "4 · distinct"]
    A5 [icon: edit, label: "5 · justified — a `why` is REQUIRED\nwritten by whatever produced it, NEVER by a human step (D-040)"]
  }
  Regr [shape: cylinder, icon: database, label: "suite/regression/ — the second manifest\nONE writer, ever: `touchstone suite admit` (loop/suite.py)\n⚠ NOT symmetric with suite/benchmark/, which has NO writer at all"]
  // ⛔ THE STORE RULE ABOVE FIRED ON `Regr` AND STOPPED ONE FILE SHORT. docs/07 §2 says
  //    draw EVERY store and its writer; the audit that added Regr added the manifest and
  //    left the changelog beside it undrawn, so the section showed where a case is KEPT and
  //    still not where its REASON is kept. Those are different artifacts: the manifest holds
  //    `why` as a required field per case (docs/02 §4), this holds one entry per suite
  //    VERSION — what was added, why, and what the agent could not do at the time.
  // ⚠ GENERATED, THEN REVIEWED — that is the claim, and it is why it is a store and not a
  //    label. docs/02 §5: "a hand-maintained changelog is how a reason outlives the fact."
  //    Generation is what keeps it honest; the review is what makes it worth reading.
  Log [shape: document, icon: file-text, label: "suite/CHANGELOG.md — one entry per suite VERSION\nGENERATED from the manifests by `touchstone suite log`, then REVIEWED\nwhat was added, why, and what the agent could not do at the time"]
  SOpen [icon: circle, label: "open — does NOT gate"]
  SLocked [color: red, icon: lock, label: "locked — GATES FOREVER, one-way\nset automatically on the first PROMOTED all_k"]
  SQuar [icon: pause-circle, label: "quarantined — human, reason REQUIRED"]
  SSuper [icon: edit, label: "superseded — human, the label was wrong"]
}

