// ── 14 · THE GATES THE PROJECT PASSES, NOT THE ONES THE AGENT PASSES (D-048) ─
// ⛔ EVERY GATE ABOVE IS ONE THE AGENT GOES THROUGH. These are the gates THE WORK
//    goes through, and this file had none of them: `exit gate` appeared ZERO times
//    in it, comments included, while ROADMAP.md carries four of them and 37
//    conditions. A picture that draws the machine's quality gates and not the
//    project's own is claiming the discipline runs in one direction only — and
//    this project's entire pitch is that it runs in the other one too.
//
// 🎯 THE LABELS CARRY AN EVIDENCE FRACTION, NOT A RULE LIST, and that is the
//    point of drawing them at all. Counted off ROADMAP.md: a condition is
//    MACHINE-ATTESTED if it names a command or an artifact — `touchstone doctor`,
//    a byte-identical `results/v1.json`, `uv run pytest`, a `git grep` that must
//    return nothing. 17 of 37 do. The other 20 are a person ticking a box, which
//    is the weakest evidence anywhere in this project and is INVISIBLE in a
//    checklist, because a ticked box looks identical either way.
//    ⛔ P2 IS THE WEAK ONE — 6 of 16 — AND IT IS THE GATE THAT SHIPS v0.1.0.
//    Putting the fraction on the node makes the soft gate the first thing a
//    reader sees, which a list of 16 ticks structurally cannot do.
//    ⚠ The fraction is a claim about WORDING, not about rigour: it counts
//      conditions that name something a machine can produce. A hand-ticked box
//      may still be checked carefully, and an attested one can still be attested
//      to the wrong thing (rule 19 — machine-attested means the run happened,
//      never that it was correct). It is a floor on evidence, and the direction
//      of its error is that it FLATTERS: every unnamed artifact counts against.
//
// ⚠ ROADMAP.md IS THE AUTHORITY for all 37. These nodes carry counts plus the
//   conditions that actually block; a second copy of a checkable list is exactly
//   the drift D-036 exists to stop, and it is why the other 33 are not here.
//
// ⛔ DiagGate IS DRAWN AS A DIAMOND AND SITS BEFORE THE CHAIN, because it gates
//    the START of a phase while the other four gate the END. docs/07 is titled
//    "the gate no phase starts without" and D-021 is the reason this file exists
//    — and `D-021` appeared ZERO times in it. A diagram omitting the rule that
//    requires the diagram is the most self-referential blind spot available, and
//    it survived every pass because nobody looks for the frame inside the picture.

DiagGate [shape: diamond, color: red, icon: alert-octagon, label: "STEP 0 OF EVERY PHASE — D-021, docs/07\nthe diagram, approved and committed BEFORE the first line of implementation\nevidence: diagrams/loop.png + diagrams/sequence.png + scripts/check-diagram.py — NINE milestones\napproval is EXPLICIT — silence is not approval (docs/07 §6)"]

Gates [icon: check-square, label: "14 · the four phase exit gates — 37 conditions · 17 machine-attested"] {
  P0Gate [color: green, icon: check-circle, label: "phase 0 exit — 5 conditions, 2 ATTESTED\n✅ PASSED: D-001 carries the live `touchstone doctor` output, verbatim\nthe model id came off ResultMessage.model_usage on a real call (D-033)"]
  P1Gate [color: blue, icon: check-square, label: "phase 1 exit — 9 conditions, 7 ATTESTED — the strongest gate here\nscore v1 TWICE from committed spans → byte-identical results/v1.json\n`git grep` the scorer for the agent's return type and find NOTHING (D-007)\ncase 09 — insufficient_evidence — is in the suite"]
  P2Gate [color: orange, icon: alert-triangle, label: "phase 2 exit — 16 conditions, 6 attested\nTHE WEAKEST GATE, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT SHIPS v0.1.0\n10 of 16 are a person ticking a box"]
  P3Gate [color: pink, icon: x-circle, label: "phase 3 exit — 7 conditions, 2 attested\nthe REJECTED candidate is the deliverable — a gate seen to block"]
}

