// ── 15 · THE GUARDS — scripts/, and NO phase builds any of them ──────────────
// ⛔ THIS SECTION EXISTS BECAUSE THE SAME HOLE WAS ALREADY FOUND ONCE, IN THE OTHER
//    ARTIFACT, AND NOT SWEPT ACROSS. docs/09 §9 says it in its own words: `scripts/`
//    was missing from the file map until 2026-08-16, four committed files referenced
//    by no doc at all, and the cause was structural — "this map places the files the
//    PHASES name, and nothing that only checks the work is ever named by a phase, so
//    the map could not see it by construction."
//    🎯 That sentence is true of THIS FILE word for word. Every other node here was
//    reached by walking a phase, so the guards were invisible to the same sweep for
//    the same reason, and the fix that closed it in docs/09 §9 was never applied here.
//    A correction is not applied until it is swept into every artifact that shared the
//    mechanism — and "the doc map" and "the picture" shared it exactly.
// ⚠ ONE ASYMMETRY MADE IT VISIBLE: check-diagram.py was already named on DiagGate, as
//   evidence. So one of the four guards was drawn and three were not — which reads as a
//   judgement about those three, and no such judgement was ever made.
// ⛔ NO Pn.n ON ANY OF THESE NODES, ON PURPOSE. There is no phase row to cite: a
//    `grep` of ROADMAP.md for all four returns nothing. Writing a plausible phase in
//    would be inventing a schedule, and this file's first convention is that a phase
//    colour is a claim. They are grey — "deferred, or cut" is wrong for them too, but
//    the honest reading is on the group label: built already, scheduled by nothing.
// ⚠ AND EVERY ONE OF THE FOUR IS WIRED, WHICH IS NOT TIDINESS. An unwired leaf is this
//   file's notation for an open question — that was the whole mechanism holding `ApiPy`
//   until D-052 answered it, which is why section 13 now leans on its LABEL rather than on
//   its edges. ⛔ The notation is unchanged and still live; it simply has no instance right
//   now, exactly as the purple legend row does. `p0-deps.sh` landed here
//   edgeless on the first pass and would have read as a fifth thing nobody had decided
//   on. It is decided, and it is built. The edge into P0Probe is the real ordering:
//   install, then measure. ⛔ Adding nodes to a notation means checking what the
//   notation says about the shape you added, not only about the words in the label.

Guards [color: grey, icon: shield, label: "15 · scripts/ — the tooling that checks or sets up the WORK\nfour files, ~26 KB, COMMITTED and NAMED BY NO PHASE (docs/09 §9)"] {
  CheckDiag [color: red, icon: image, label: "check-diagram.py — the D-021 guard, NINE milestones\nthe only check that reads the RENDER, not the source (7)\n8 and 9 grep the DSL for what the renderer EATS or MANGLES"]
  CheckLinks [icon: link, label: "check-links.py — every markdown link resolves\n⚠ against GIT, never the working tree — an empty dir passes on disk and 404s in public"]
  P0Probe [icon: search, label: "p0-probe.py — the two phase 0 measurements\ndocs/00 §8 requires them BEFORE code"]
  P0Deps [icon: download, label: "p0-deps.sh — the phase 0 install, ONE command"]
}

CheckDiag > DiagGate: the evidence D-021 asks for
P0Probe > P0Gate: 2 measurements, taken before the first line
CheckLinks --> Gates: runs against every gate's citations — blocks none of them
P0Deps > P0Probe: install first — there is nothing to measure until it is installed

// ── THE OPEN QUESTIONS — NONE OPEN, AND THE TWO CLOSED 2026-08-18 ────────────
// ✅ BOTH WERE ANSWERED BY THE READER, WHICH IS THE ONLY PLACE EITHER COULD HAVE
//    BEEN ANSWERED — one was a scope call and one was a notation call, and this
//    file is allowed to make neither on its own.
//      · api.py — CUT (D-052). Section 13's node is grey and says what cut it.
//      · green — the KEY gave way (D-053): "phase 0 — shipped, or a good outcome".
//        The nodes kept their colour; the row now documents the second meaning.
// ⛔ THE HISTORY BELOW IS KEPT VERBATIM AND IS NOT DECORATION. Both questions
//    were invisible to a sweep, for two DIFFERENT reasons, and those reasons
//    outlive the answers — the next question will hide the same two ways.
//
// ⚠ SO THE COUNT IS CURRENTLY ZERO, AND ZERO IS THE READING THIS FILE DISTRUSTS
//   MOST. docs/07 §6: "a diagram with no open questions is usually a diagram
//   nobody thought about." It is honest here only because both answers arrived as
//   decisions with IDs, in one sitting, from the person entitled to make them.
//   ⛔ If this section still says zero several passes from now, that is evidence
//   nobody has looked, not evidence the design is settled.
//
// ── the record of how each one hid ───────────────────────────────────────────
// docs/07 §6: a diagram with no open questions is usually a diagram nobody
// thought about. The three this started with are closed — D-037 (the scorer
// reads spans from phase 1), D-038 (v1 IS the synthesizer node), D-039 (the
// bound is 6). ⛔ THAT IS THE GOOD OUTCOME, NOT A MISSING SECTION. D-038 says
// it explicitly: an "open" question nothing is waiting on is a decision with
// the record missing, and leaving it drawn as open was a rejected option.
//
// 🔴 QUESTION ONE — CLOSED BY D-052, AND THIS IS HOW IT HID. The heading here
//    read "and why the list is now empty" and that was FALSE: one question was
//    open, it was section 13's `ApiPy`, and the node has said so
//    in its own label the whole time: whether api.py is built at all, after
//    D-040 removed the durable interrupt that was its only justification
//    (ROADMAP P2.8, docs/06 header). The file therefore contained a completeness
//    claim and, four sections above it, the counter-example — and the claim was
//    the more confident of the two. ⚠ The failure was not a stale comment. The
//    three closed questions were closed by DECISIONS, so "closed" was checked
//    against D-037/D-038/D-039; this one was never opened by a decision, it was
//    opened by one being REVERSED, so nothing in the D-series marked it. A
//    question created by a withdrawal is invisible to a sweep that looks for
//    questions created by a decision.
//    🎯 It is now COUNTABLE rather than asserted: a question ABOUT A NODE is the
//    node, painted purple. Empty list ⟺ no purple in the legend's sense.
//
// 🔴 QUESTION TWO — CLOSED BY D-053, AND IT BROKE THE RULE ONE LINE ABOVE ON
//    THE SAME PASS THAT WROTE IT. Convention 1 was checked against the DSL and found false; the
//    correction surfaced a live question with it: `green` is keyed "phase 0 —
//    shipped" and sits on `Scored` and `Promoted`, the two good OUTCOMES.
//    ⚠ SWEPT 2026-08-17. This said "the only node naming a P0 artifact (`CliPy`)
//      is blue"; `DoctorPy` now exists, is phase 0, has shipped, and is green by
//      the key. The question is unchanged and SHARPER — green is on one real P0
//      node and two outcomes at once — so what was a colour with no true instance
//      is now a colour with a true instance and two false ones. Either the
//      outcomes give it up, or the key stops claiming a phase. ✅ ANSWERED
//      2026-08-18: the key gave way, not the nodes — D-053, and the cost of that
//      choice is stated in convention 1 rather than hidden here.
//    ⛔ IT CANNOT BE PAINTED PURPLE, and that is the finding, not a snag. It is
//    a question about the KEY — about what a colour means — so there is no node
//    to colour, and painting one would state the question in the very notation
//    the question is about. **A question about the notation is invisible to a
//    count that is taken in that notation.** Same shape as the paragraph above:
//    that one escaped a sweep for questions-opened-by-a-decision because it was
//    opened by a WITHDRAWAL; this one escapes a sweep for purple nodes because
//    it is not about a node. Both times the mechanism was sound and the
//    ENUMERATION it ran over was the thing with the hole in it.
//    ⚠ So the honest rule is two-part, and the second part is not mechanical:
//    purple nodes, PLUS whatever is written in this section. If those two ever
//    disagree, this section wins — it is the one a person maintains.
//
// ⚠ WHAT REPLACES IT IS NOT A FOURTH QUESTION — IT IS THE FALSIFIER OF THE
//   ONE ANSWER THAT IS NOT A MEASUREMENT. 6 was chosen with no run behind it,
//   because the first run IS v2, so there was never a version that did not
//   already depend on the answer. The picture therefore carries the rule that
//   keeps it honest rather than the number, which lives in one place:
//     · TOO SMALL is caught by `hops_exhausted` — the ceiling fired instead of
//       the supervisor stopping, read off the last supervisor span's `next`.
//     · TOO LARGE is already caught by `cost_per_correct_usd`, a promotion
//       metric, because a supervisor with spare budget wanders.
//   Two directions, two detectors, neither of them new machinery.
//
// ⛔ RED, NOT GREY. Grey is "deferred, or cut" in the key and this is neither —
//    the old node was grey while it was an open question, which the key never
//    covered. Red is "an invariant, or a never", and the never is exact: never
//    re-run a version at a different bound and report the better number.

